## 3. The thirteen C7–C9 entries

The table maps each name added by hand in `9d80934e` to what needs it and to the three checks.
"Imported" is membership in the `libcamel.dll` block of `graph.cmo`'s import table; `.def` and PE
are membership in the generated file and in the DLL's export table. All comparisons are
case-sensitive.

| # | Decorated name (short) | graph.cmo imports | in `.def` | in PE | call site in the module |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `?commitChecked@RuntimeGraphDraftSession...` | yes | yes | yes | `txn.cpp:242` — `commit` |
| 2 | `?currentRuntimeProgram@Context...` | yes | yes | yes | `module.cpp:77` — `current` |
| 3 | `?graphSpace@mm...` | yes | yes | yes | `handle.cpp:156`, `txn.cpp:94` |
| 4 | `?isReplaceable@generic...` | yes | yes | yes | `txn.cpp:190,210` — `replace`/`erase` |
| 5 | `?nodeAttrs@GCGraph...` | **no** | **no** | **no** | none in the module |
| 6 | `?nodeRef@GCGraph...` | yes | yes | yes | `read.cpp:243` — `nodes` |
| 7 | `?prototype@EnumDecl...` | yes | yes | yes | `nodekind.cpp:60`, `regionkind.cpp:53` |
| 8 | `?reaches@generic...` | yes | yes | yes | `txn.cpp:196` — `replace` |
| 9 | `?replaceNode@generic...` | yes | yes | yes | `txn.cpp:202,222` |
| 10 | `?returnNodeRef@GCGraph...` | yes | yes | yes | `read.cpp:464` — `is_anchor` |
| 11 | `?segmentOf@GrowableFreeListAllocator...` | yes | yes | yes | the inline `contains` at `include/camel/core/mm/alloc/growable.h:180`, called by the `graphSpace().isAllocated` checks |
| 12 | `?text@attr...` | yes | yes | yes | `read.cpp:448` — `tags` |
| 13 | `?toString@fact...` | yes | yes | yes | `facts.cpp:106` — `shape` |

Twelve of the thirteen are exactly what the module imports, and both configurations export them.
`nodeAttrs` is the exception: the module never calls it. It is defined in libcamel and used only
inside libcamel (`src/core/tags.cpp` and the draft/graph runtime files are the libcamel objects that
reference it), so no dependent object names it and a generated list correctly omits it. The old hand
list exported it although nothing outside libcamel needed it; nothing needs it now either. This is
not a spelling mismatch.

**Which spelling is correct, and why.** There is no independent spelling to choose: the decorated
name is emitted by clang from the declaration, and `graph.cmo`'s import table and `libcamel.dll`'s
export table carry the identical byte string for all 112 (Release) / 113 (Debug) symbols. The
thirteen hand names no longer exist in the tree; the only entries in
`cmake/libcamel_exports_manual.def` are the standalone bridge and `printSlotCapped`, neither of them
a graph symbol. Nothing is special-cased for Windows.

## 4. The module loads, and every entry is called by its Camel name

Probe `D:\Temp\H35\h35_exports.cml` imports `graph` and calls the three C8 entries (`effects`,
`shape`, `permissions`) and the four C7 entries (`open_function`, `to_function`, `graph_of`,
`program_of`) by name. It prints:

```
false
[-, -, -, -, f32 [1, 3]]
[0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
target
5
__root__
```

Line by line: `effects(grid).external` is false; `shape` over the grid graph's nodes has one tensor
(`f32 [1, 3]`, the reshape node); `permissions` are 0; `graph_of(target)` is `target`; the
`open_function` / `to_function` round trip gives a function value that returns 5 for 5;
`program_of(target)` is the running program, whose entry graph is `__root__`. Exit 0 under both
`Camel v0.2.24 (Build 261021_132044_v0.2.23_84_gcc0a6deb)` and
`Camel v0.2.24 (Debug 261021_133013_v0.2.23_84_gcc0a6deb_dirty)`.

The same seven lines from an ordinary program that imports the module mean the module was found,
loaded, and its operator groups registered; a missing or misspelled libcamel export would have
stopped it at load time, and a missing kernel would fail the call.

