## 6. Debug build

`-Config Debug` finished green: 366 targets, 84 s, exit 0, with
`[329/366] Generating libcamel exports for Debug...` and
`[332/362] Linking CXX shared library modules\graph\Debug\graph.cmo`. The Debug `.def` has 522 names
(520 derived + 2 manual); the Debug DLL's PE table has 528. `graph.cmo` imports 113 symbols, one more
than Release: `?assertStoredValueIsNotView@rtdata@core@camel...`, the view-escape assertion that
exists only in a Debug build (H30). All 113 are in the Debug `.def` and in the Debug PE table
(0 missing), and the 112 Release imports are a subset. The Debug probe prints the same seven lines
and the Debug plan is 47/47, so the same symbols link, load and run in Debug.

## 7. What changed

* `test/cases/modules/graph_program.cml` (new), its entry `program_of_a_function_value` in the plan,
  and one line in the AST snapshot — the automation the task asked for. It would catch a future
  loader/kernel failure of `program_of`; a spelling mismatch itself is caught earlier, by the link
  of `graph.cmo` against the generated `.def`.
* No declaration and no export table changed: every name the module imports was already exported
  in Release and Debug, and the generated list covers it.

The verification script is `D:\Temp\H35\verify_graph_exports.ps1` (scratch, not committed: it
hard-codes this worktree and the LLVM path; the durable check is the link itself plus the plan).

## 8. Open questions

* `docs/handover/reports/H40-export-list.md` §5 says the generated list reproduces "the 13 graph
  symbols". It reproduces twelve; `nodeAttrs` is imported by no dependent object and is exported in
  neither configuration. That is correct behaviour, but the sentence in that report is one too
  broad. I left that other report untouched; this is the correction.
* Why the hand list of `9d80934e` included `nodeAttrs` at all is not recorded. It may have been
  inferred from libcamel's own object references. With a generated list the question is closed.
* The workstation's shared lock (`Global\CamelWorkSerialized`) can be left abandoned when a holder
  is killed; one H35 test run exited 1 before starting with
  `The wait completed due to an abandoned mutex.` The coordinator fixed both helpers to catch
  `AbandonedMutexException` and treat the wait as acquired; after that the Debug run above went
  through.
